<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>3 years on, Morocco earthquake victims still wait for help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:278b59db5a76ce071b38eeebf58914b6a2817278c350ca8f746d1948f9ec4123</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844--12aebab2298e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reconstruction has progressed in the three years since the 2023 Morocco earthquake, but some survivors are still living in tents. Locals are divided as to how successful it's been, and whether state aid is enough.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c388abbb4171042f1d1173ef20d74055a4e7c27b0af7a97b754efdb7ff16b33</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0809fba5927a8ec7201fb8385eccacd75bccf193f69bbb33110d8d048cb1a9c</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Germany wakes up to 'unsettling' AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0dc58863cd35ee1660e42bfbd7c3f02ea826c5949477daf7b7cc549f449539</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934--2d9595de9f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party won the Saxony-Anhalt state election but without an absolute majority in parliament. Other European nations were wrestling with the impact of the results. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can the AfD form a government in Saxony-Anhalt?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03b9d99258ba2fddacd590fdf638667ed2e45453ad329aac3a668707f841fecf</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-afd-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79107331--72d013c68919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-afd-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record election success, the far-right Alternative for Germany aims to form a government. What options does it have without the absolute majority?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia announces it is closing Germany's consulate in St. Petersburg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32bc30b55108a86c8200a215453c28d180c26aa6b5531e11b21a1599adfff478</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-announces-it-is-closing-germany-s-consulate-in-st-petersburg/a-79149908--0c758ae8cdb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-announces-it-is-closing-germany-s-consulate-in-st-petersburg/a-79149908?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tit-for-tat reaction comes after Germany said it is shutting down Russia's consulate in Bonn and its cultural center in Berlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96d7411a3727128bf45efe07e30037877cb1665e0979c878f7ebf39f22a88db6</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Chancellor Merz says AfD result 'changes all of Germany'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:133b9cf6555eba328697b1313d024cd74c8564e6b8a93e073e7ebdf309db3450</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560--fdb0b7e42c28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visibly shaken but also determined Friedrich Merz spoke in Berlin about the AfD's election victory in Saxony-Anhalt and the CDU's bitter defeat. He insisted on sticking to his reforms.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Carbon capture tech exists. Scaling it up is the hard part</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c8e078bd62d73508283d6c1bf76e502ae0e4dcea3469b01c26378cd28ce8266</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/carbon-capture-tech-exists-scaling-it-up-is-the-hard-part/a-79147600--ed63d6043f0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/carbon-capture-tech-exists-scaling-it-up-is-the-hard-part/a-79147600?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe just opened a carbon capture and storage plant billed as the continent's largest. But global climate scenarios call for far more capacity than exists anywhere on Earth.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Can creating new provinces fix governance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f39e75aab0d5198ded7983ee82fb398bcd6ac52830dbcf6f0f21ff55dbb86229</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059--3974ef70363a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistanis broadly agree that the country needs more responsive and effective government, but many question whether simply creating more provinces is the solution.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU's von der Leyen pledges $232 million Greenland investment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32c913073c2d547b2c152eb55f62300319a12a4450ef9e5452e7e95e116f61a3</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-von-der-leyen-pledges-232-million-greenland-investment/a-79109197--af8beb0f9327.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-von-der-leyen-pledges-232-million-greenland-investment/a-79109197?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is preparing a major investment package and closer political ties with the Danish Arctic territory amid Donald Trump's demand for greater US control of the mineral-rich island.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Threatening letters revive fears among Kashmiri Pandits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:515275ef26bbdafab53c8c84416c6d31549669670a2a32233d1b72700e1ec3f9</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481--ac4e07371076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaked addresses and phone numbers have reignited fears among Hindu government employees who returned to Muslim-majority Kashmir under a rehabilitation scheme.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia opens first road bridge with North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:475c3050998feec7278a955b3b92bd40b42fc2dcfe6bc0952c71a041e228e21f</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-opens-first-road-bridge-with-north-korea/a-79142595--dfd907ad5594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-opens-first-road-bridge-with-north-korea/a-79142595?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia and North Korea have opened their first road bridge across the Tumen River as political, economic and military ties between the two countries deepen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Israeli strikes kill a dozen in Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a6515de49ce53f209d818e09046b9f8f88ef3b602eebdb81770a28e29e44942</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:02:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-east-israeli-strikes-kill-a-dozen-in-lebanon/live-79133242--8dc16e4cc465.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-israeli-strikes-kill-a-dozen-in-lebanon/live-79133242?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lebanon's Health Ministry said at least 12 were killed in overnight Israeli strikes in the south of the country. Meanwhile, traffic in the Strait of Hormuz has sunk to its lowest level since May.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says war looks set to go on into winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057b215b1615dca06a542a17dae0ebce6681dff26aa06cdea5c099c1ca54a8e8</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-war-looks-set-to-go-on-into-winter/live-79135930--33643c7a4b0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-war-looks-set-to-go-on-into-winter/live-79135930?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy says there appears to be no end in sight in Russia's war against his country. His words come after another round of US-led diplomacy. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK government condemns 'thuggish' anti-migrant protests in Portsmouth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b30fff3eea44a4bd47ead12f4e340d8d027ca0df70c46f88dcfde5729ca7a9bf</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-government-condemns-thuggish-anti-migrant-protests-in-portsmouth/a-79134048--212251740773.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-government-condemns-thuggish-anti-migrant-protests-in-portsmouth/a-79134048?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds gathered in Portsmouth after some refugees arrived by boat from France, a day after masked protesters disrupted traffic at the port of Dover.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rescue efforts underway in deadly Delhi building collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34401f25c8dee1ba56b4b453b2d41582514dc6dc1cdc7b5beb4e71a6054ae318</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rescue-efforts-underway-in-deadly-delhi-building-collapse/live-79123607--5263e9e58a28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rescue-efforts-underway-in-deadly-delhi-building-collapse/live-79123607?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The building was located in New Delhi's Satya Niketan, popular among students from nearby colleges and universities. At least 12 people have been rescued from the rubble.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica to petition King Charles over slavery reparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4793f0e4e888867c110f4156528ed80ad856197aa1e26fbdc038a3f6a539556c</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jamaica-to-petition-king-charles-over-slavery-reparations/a-79123536--34efcede7988.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jamaica-to-petition-king-charles-over-slavery-reparations/a-79123536?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jamaica will ask King Charles III to refer questions about the legality of slavery and Britain's potential obligation to provide reparations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Amazon cargo plane crash in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7718cfa192930b208f588794dc638a604e9dddc83f42ceeedcb5d9fff1f0e2b2</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T23:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365--4869fc3bcedd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least five people have died after a cargo plane crashed at Miami International Airport. The aircraft overran a runway, struck several vehicles and caught fire.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db568c2736ae68dace514436b500366895400fb9a6fd12ae8e775b07c3f0684</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea3744d4b0d92916096e1092f540c14cd22a6feca65f066770781afb22f29085</id><updated>2026-09-07T20:01:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
